WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:02.210
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.790
<i>Do you know about the
"most beautiful formula in mathematics history"?</i>

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.090
<i>It's eiπ+1=0, what people call Euler's Identity</i>.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.680
<i>The natural logarithmic base e,</i>

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.140
<i>the ratio of circumference to diameter pi,
the imaginary number i, 1, and 0</i>

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.520
<i>all fit into this equation with nothing superfluous,
and fit in such a way that it was meant to be.</i>

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.560
<i>If there is a god in this world,</i>

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.780
<i>this is a piece of evidence
that will be listed as one of the most credible.</i>

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:29.650
WHAT'S AMUSING, OR AT LEAST BEAUTIFUL,
IS THAT THIS FORMULA WAS "PREDETERMINED."

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:30.610
IT'S BEAUTIFUL,
BUT WHEN YOU THINK ABOUT IT, IT'S ALSO SCARY.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:36.870
<i>And yet, Ougi Oshino - that transfer student -
just might throw out some candid advice</i>

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.660
<i>even for the beauty of Euler's Identity,
just like this:</i>

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.330
Yes. It indeed is beautiful, Araragi-senpai.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.130
Beautiful, so beautiful,
it just makes me swoon.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.050
The most beautiful part about it
is that the answer is zero.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.260
That said, someone like me thinks
that if the answer is going to be zero

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.760
there's really no need
to go out of your way to make the calculation.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.930
<i>Hearing that, I reconfirm my belief;</i>

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:07.270
<i>Ougi Oshino is Ougi Oshino,
and there's no way to express it.</i>

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.030
<i>Before her, everything is zero.</i>

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.150
<i>No matter what she does
that may seem out of character,</i>

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.110
<i>it always ends up
being something characteristic of her.</i>

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.030
<i>And so, this time,
we have a story about mathematics.</i>

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.780
<i>Let's study.</i>

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:23.460
<i>People tend to brace themselves
when they hear "mathematics".</i>

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.080
<i>So we can break it down
and say this is a story about "arithmetic" instead.</i>

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.500
<i>While we're at it, we can be more blunt
and say this is a story about "numbers."</i>

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.470
<i>After all, this is a story
where strength in numbers provides a solution.</i>

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.340
<i>In other words,
it's a story about majority rule.</i>

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.050
<i>Majority rule.</i>

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:43.180
<i>The only method that can
turn even a mistake into a truth.</i>

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:48.310
<i>A formula of building blocks
that pursues conspiring instead of happiness.</i>

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.690
<i>Our inequality. Our unfair equation.</i>

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.030
INEQUALITY

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:52.780
UNFAIR EQUATION

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:57.490
<i>What can truly be said as something humanity
has invented is probably this and only this.</i>

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:01.790
<i>And, this is the ugliest formula
in human history.</i>

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.000
OUGI FORMULA, PART ONE

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.380
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:41.680
<i>If you were with
an underclassman you've just met,</i>

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.890
<i>and you found yourselves trapped within a mysterious
classroom, and an hour had already passed...</i>

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.640
<i>If you've ever had such an experience,
I'd definitely like to seek your advice.</i>

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:53.060
It's no good, Araragi-senpai.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.570
Oh, that just now...
I didn't mean that you're no good at all, okay?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:01.780
I've tried lots of things, but neither the
big windows or the upper ones will budge one bit.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.530
That's what I meant.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:05.830
No...

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.200
A misunderstanding
where I feel like I'm no good?

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.920
I hardly think this is a situation
where I could do that.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.500
It's no good on my end either.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.210
It doesn't feel like they're locked or anything...

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:22.340
Somehow, it feels more like they're held in place
by something like glue.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:26.680
Yes. Just like I said before,
the window will not budge, even a tiny bit.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:31.310
As for the locks, the crescent locks
that are fixtures of these windows do move.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.690
However, the actual window frames don't move.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:40.940
Right, so it "feels more like" they're held in place
by something like a glue.

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:46.530
We have no choice.
Let's wait for help from outside, Ougi.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:50.370
Fortunately, the fact that we're here
is something Kanbaru knows about.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:51.620
I don't know about that.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.420
You're relying on someone else
to help you, Araragi-senpai?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:58.500
All people can do
is save themselves on their own.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.050
Yet...

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.090
Excuse me.
This was a principle that my uncle used.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.350
It has nothing to do with me
or with you, Araragi-senpai.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:14.600
But in any case, Araragi-senpai,
it's not a bad thing to rely on one's comrades.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:21.280
But fundamentally, I don't think we should give up
trying to escape by our own strength.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.490
Because...

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:30.290
<i>The hands of the clock,
from the moment we entered this classroom...</i>

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:33.540
<i>They hadn't moved a minute...
not even a second.</i>

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:38.540
Out of batteries?
I don't think it'd be anything like that.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.540
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.420
<i>Everything began on a certain day
at the end of October,</i>

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:42.630
NAOETSU HIGH SCHOOL

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.090
<i>roughly six months since spring break,</i>

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:49.550
<i>when I was assaulted by a vampire
with blonde hair and golden eyes.</i>

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:52.850
Hey, Araragi-senpai!
It's me, Suruga Kanbaru!

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.640
Are you alone? Yeah, you're alone!

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:58.060
Actually, there's someone
I want to introduce to you, Araragi-senpai!

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.690
Isn't she cute?

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.240
So, what's with that girl?
You said you wanted to introduce her to me...

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.280
She said she had something she wanted advice about.
From you, Araragi-senpai.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.530
So I want you to go meet her.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.990
So, what's this advice that she wants?

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:18.460
I didn't hear all the details either,
but it's apparently some advice about apparitions.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.550
Yeah, it somehow seems like
she knows something.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:27.090
She knew about my left hand,
and also about your blood, Araragi-senpai.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.100
She said she heard them all from her uncle.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:30.970
Uncle...

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:34.720
She's a first-year that transferred into this school
just the other day.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:38.730
Surprisingly enough,
she's apparently the niece of old Oshino.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:42.320
Her name is Ougi Oshino.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.110
This is strange.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.450
Strange.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:51.030
It is mysterious.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:52.780
Mysterious.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.790
In other words... It's suspicious.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:56.580
Suspicious...

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:57.620
<i>...and different.</i>

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.500
This is strange...

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:09.550
Um, will you listen to me, Araragi-senpai?

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:10.760
Oh, well...

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:14.310
Too many school buildings,
or something like that?

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:19.020
Like how you can save costs enough for one whole building
if you think about the total number of students...

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:22.770
That's not it at all.
Are you a fool or something?

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.320
This is where I'm talking about.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:27.280
Where?

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.860
Here. The layout is a bit odd here.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.370
I guess more unnatural than odd?

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:35.830
See, look at the floors
right above and right below it.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.330
Each of them have proper rooms here, right?

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:43.460
Then, this place which is in-between both of them
needs to have a room here, or it ends up being strange.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.590
Strange...

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:50.380
AUDIOVISUAL ROOM

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.010
That's because the floor plan is mistaken.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:57.520
Instead of mistaken,
more like it was drawn based on reality,

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:00.390
but the actual audiovisual room
isn't this long.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:06.020
Compared to the others, it's drawn to be about
1.5 times longer than it actually is. Don't you notice it?

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:11.950
What's this? By any chance,
do you doubt me, Araragi-senpai?

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:15.410
It hurts me that
you'd doubt me, Araragi-senpai.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:19.950
No, you don't like me enough
to be hurt by me doubting you.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:25.540
No, no... I do fancy you quite a bit.
I fancy the fool that is easily deceived.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:32.510
In mystery novels, when the floor plan
and reality don't match like this...

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:36.050
A majority of the cases ends up
having a hidden room at that location.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:41.600
However, if this is some sort of phenomenon
caused by an apparition...

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:45.980
I thought it'd be better to investigate
before there's any damage done by it.

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.440
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:01.250
What? I wonder what this classroom is.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:06.630
When I walked by here to make the floorplan,
this place didn't exist.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.130
Such a mystery!

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:11.630
In any case... Let's try going in.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:29.270
And that's how we got to where we are now.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:31.900
What do you think about this, Araragi-senpai?

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:35.240
What do I think?
Well, nothing of any note, really.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:40.830
But Ougi, if this was a phenomenon
caused by an apparition... what kind of apparition is it?

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:46.540
Who knows? Unlike my uncle,
I don't have much quaint knowledge.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:49.040
I only know about the major apparitions
that show up in manga and in movies.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.550
OUGI / KOYOMI

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:53.920
But, Araragi-senpai,
there is one thing I can say.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:58.430
That is, an apparition has a reason
befitting it behind it...

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:00.970
WHICH MEANS, UNRAVELING THE REASON WHY
WILL LEAD TO OUR ESCAPE FROM HERE.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.940
Even so, what meaning is behind this situation
where we can't get out of this classroom?

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.850
And about how the clock has stopped, too.

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:11.690
Perhaps the clock being stopped
is the key to all this, surprisingly enough?

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:16.110
Because it showing such a random time
does give a feeling of wrongness after all, right?

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:19.740
Speaking of 6:00PM, that's when
we have to leave this high school campus.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:23.040
At a time when students
must go home from their classrooms,

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.960
this phenomenon locks students
inside the classroom.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.250
What's the meaning behind it?

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.710
It's time to leave school,
but not being allowed to go home...

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:34.960
I guess you could call it
an overtime class or something?

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:36.260
Overtime...

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:40.350
Have you ever had it before, Araragi-senpai?

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.430
An experience of taking
overtime supplementary lessons.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:48.940
I may look like this, but I do have pretty good brains,
so I don't recall anything much like that.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:50.400
Me neither.

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.900
Oh, is that so?

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:56.530
<i>In my case, even if I'm told to stay overtime
or to take supplementary lessons,</i>

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.320
<i>I end up ditching most of them.</i>

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:03.160
<i>But, yeah, last year, or two years ago...
especially when I was a first-year.</i>

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.750
<i>Back when I was a first-year?</i>

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.670
What's wrong, Araragi-senpai?

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:14.050
Your flag color looks a bit off...
no wait, your facial color is a bit pale.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:18.170
Is that so? Sorry,
I just had a slight dizzy spell.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:22.430
No need to apologize. Not at all.
You don't have to apologize.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:25.680
I'm sure that with an unreliable underclassman
before you so, your nerves must be strained.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.430
Perhaps you've gotten a bit tired?

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:30.310
How about you sit in one of those chairs?

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.120
Why did you sit there?

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:50.250
What? You ask me why, but...
Wasn't it because you recommended it, Ougi?

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:54.590
No, no, I mean...
There are a lot of chairs in this classroom.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:56.880
I'm asking why you chose that seat.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:00.970
I just felt like it.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:03.970
You just felt like it?
That seat was easy to sit at?

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:05.930
It looked like it was going to be
comfortable sitting there?

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:11.270
No, how comfortable it is won't change much
no matter which chair you pick, I think...

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:12.690
But, well...

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.020
But, well?

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.400
I'm used to sitting here.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:18.650
That's how I felt.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.860
Is that true?

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:24.660
What? What was that, Ougi?

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.910
No, I am merely going through
every single possibility.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:33.910
One possibility is that perhaps you, Araragi-senpai,
sat in that chair in the past.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:38.920
So once it came time to settle down into a seat,
can it be that you chose that seat without hesitation?

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.800
No, that's way too wild an idea.

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:46.300
Until just now, I didn't even know
that there was a classroom in this location.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:50.140
As for me, when I investigated
around here for the first time,

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:52.230
a classroom like this didn't exist.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:57.110
However, when I came here with you,
Araragi-senpai, this classroom appeared.

00:12:57.110 --> 00:13:02.700
Then, to think that this classroom is somehow
associated with you is something very natural to me.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.320
I guess that's how it works out.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:08.580
Besides, you said so yourself,
Araragi-senpai...

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:12.620
that you somehow felt like
you've seen the scenery from this window.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:14.540
Did I say such a thing?

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:19.710
You did. Right when we entered the classroom,
before we realized we'd been locked in here.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:26.220
<i>I don't recall saying so...
But since she clearly asserts so, I'm sure I did say it.</i>

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:29.760
<i>It's true that somehow...</i>

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.100
<i>My memory... is being stimulated.</i>

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.720
My oh my. What's wrong, Araragi-senpai?

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:06.760
It doesn't seem like
you came up with an idea.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:09.680
Perhaps I said something
without picking up some hint?

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:13.480
Something you didn't want to remember...
have you remembered something of that sort?

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:18.190
No, it's not something like that.
There's nothing that came back into my memory.

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:21.650
<i>That's right...
Nothing has come back into my memory.</i>

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:25.200
<i>Because... I've never forgotten about it at all.</i>

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.450
<i>Because there's no way
I can forget an incident like that.</i>

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.700
CLASS 1-3 / KOYOMI ARARAGI

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:35.460
What? Wasn't that textbook labeled "Araragi"?

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:38.790
That's strange, that's mysterious.
Why is that so?

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:41.840
Why is Araragi-senpai's textbook
inside this classroom?

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:46.260
Ougi... Do you know something?

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.890
I don't know anything.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:50.760
You're the one that knows.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:15:02.150
Ougi, is there anything
that can tell today's date around there?

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:03.480
The date, you say?

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:09.410
Yeah, today... No, I mean the date in this classroom.
I want to know what it is.

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:12.620
Something like that's
written on the blackboard.

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:13.870
Please take a look. See?

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.620
JULY 15 (THU)

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:20.130
Whoa. It was July 15th today.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:24.000
Then, is it adequate to think of it like this?

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:30.090
In this classroom, on Thursday, July 15th,
around 6:00PM, something happened...

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:33.050
And I'm sure it was something
full of resentment.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:36.640
And that resentment, like this,
has solidified into the form of an apparition.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:38.020
There's no doubt about it.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:45.610
<i>That classroom on the fifth floor
of the building facing the gym.</i>

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.940
<i>Class 1-3 was right in the middle,</i>

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:50.910
<i>and after school on July 15th
a class assembly was being held.</i>

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.320
<i>A class assembly that you could call a trial.</i>

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.290
<i>Concerning a certain incident,
we denounced each other.</i>

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:04.420
<i>And I, Koyomi Araragi from class 1-3,
was at the center of said trial.</i>

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:09.970
<i>That's right. Wasn't it since that very day
that I started to say something of that nature?</i>

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.180
"I don't need friends.

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:15.430
If I make friends,
my strength as a human decreases."

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:19.600
It was your pet phrase,
wasn't it, Araragi-senpai?

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:22.190
Though, ever since you had that experience
with Ms. Tsubasa Hanekawa,

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:24.310
you apparently never said it again.

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:29.280
Well, meeting people does change people, I guess.

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.030
Then, I shall ask out of curiosity.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:35.450
In this classroom, in what way,
Araragi-senpai, did you change?

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:40.080
The folks in class 1-3...
How did they change you?

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.210
Change... me...

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:45.250
I heard that the you in middle school
and the you in high school

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:47.920
have drastically different personalities,
you know?

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:51.970
The reason behind it, perhaps,
is right here in this classroom?

00:16:54.010 --> 00:17:00.100
What happened, Araragi-senpai?
In this classroom, that day, that moment...

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:04.190
Let's just talk about it, Araragi-senpai.

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:05.730
Koyomi Araragi.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.360
You'll feel at ease once you talk about it.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:12.150
No matter how horrible the memory,
after it all comes out it becomes just a story.

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:14.110
A story...

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:16.780
It's fine. I'll listen to it for you.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:20.500
I may look like this,
but I am pretty understanding of things.

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:25.540
We can't get out.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:26.580
Yes?

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.250
We can't get out.

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:32.470
Until we know who the culprit was,
we're not allowed to leave this classroom.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:38.510
What we did... what we forced upon ourselves...
was a class assembly of that sort.

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:44.980
It may be a story hard to believe...
But there, I was the one presiding over the assembly.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:48.270
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:49.480
TWO YEARS AGO

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:00.370
<i>Her name was Sodachi Oikura.</i>

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:05.250
<i>She herself wanted to be called "Euler",
but in reality everyone called her "How much".</i>

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.540
<i>I'm sure it was a nickname
that came from her last name,</i>

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:12.050
<i>but because she looks at others
as though appraising them,</i>

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:14.760
<i>I think it was strangely appropriate.</i>

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.010
SODACHI OIKURA

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:19.600
Prez Oikura.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.890
Were you the one that called for me?

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:26.390
Hurry up and get in here.
Everyone's been waiting for you.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:38.780
<i>Inside the classroom,
the members of class 1-3 were all present.</i>

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.160
<i>Not one person was missing.</i>

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:40.660
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:44.910
So, everyone, huh...
So I guess you have full members.

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:52.340
Right now, this is an empty classroom as you can see,
but then, every seat had been taken, huh?

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:56.930
I see, I see. Time flies like an arrow.
They say ten years can feel like one day.

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:57.090
TEN YEARS (CAN FEEL LIKE) ONE DAY

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:59.260
Yeah... No, but it's not ten years,
it's only two years.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:00.430
TWO YEARS (CAN FEEL LIKE) ONE DAY

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:04.970
Well, if we start talking about details,
Oikura was standing at the teacher's desk.

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:06.690
On top of the teacher's desk?

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:09.440
Oikura wasn't that strange a class president.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:13.440
Anyway, she was standing at the teacher's desk,
and made the declaration:

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:17.450
"Now, we will begin our special class assembly."

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:20.990
But that's rather mysterious.

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:24.370
Araragi-senpai, you didn't know that
this class assembly was being held

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.450
until right before it started, right?

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:30.080
That was simply a mistake
in relaying information, apparently.

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:33.710
Everyone in class was supposed to get
some kind of a network message that day,

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:37.720
whether it be a folded-up note, a text,
or stuff like that going around the class.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:41.220
But not one of them reached me.

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:47.230
That's... What you would call the lone wolf?

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:48.600
That's somewhat a misunderstanding.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:49.520
IT'S NOT A COMPLETE MISUNDERSTANDING, THOUGH.
KOYOMI ARARAGI = LONE WOLF

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:53.150
Ougi, this is a story of the process

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:56.400
in which someone with no friends
ends up not needing any friends.

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:59.490
Then, let me take a proper posture as I listen to it.

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:01.780
To this story about some special class assembly
or something like that.

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:04.780
Of today's discussion topic
at the class assembly...

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.000
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:09.120
<i>First off, Oikura brought this subject up:</i>

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:11.830
Today's topic is "figuring out the culprit."

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:16.090
Until we figure out the culprit,
or until the culprit speaks up on his own behalf,

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:19.630
I won't allow anyone out of this classroom.
Prepare yourselves for that.

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:27.220
<i>I confirmed the seat of Hitagi Senjyogahara.</i>

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:29.430
<i>She was very frail in health,</i>

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:32.400
<i>and my image of her was that she didn't
come to school for even half of the first term.</i>

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:38.110
<i>Even she was here like this, so it could be assumed
that the situation was very serious.</i>

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.820
"Figuring out the culprit"...

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:44.410
That doesn't sound too peaceful.
What in the world had happened?

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:44.780
CURRICULUM SCHEDULE

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:47.660
After school on the day
before final exams began,

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:47.910
we had asked for volunteers and held
a study group for mathematics in the classroom.

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:51.410
TEST SCHEDULE

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:52.120
INFORMATION ABOUT A STUDY GROUP

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:54.920
Apparently Oikura had participated
in this study group.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:57.050
I see, a study group.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:20:57.210
TEST RESULTS

00:20:57.210 --> 00:21:01.380
But after the exams were over,
there was a discrepancy averaging 20 points

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:06.550
between those that participated in this study group,
and those that didn't.

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:11.940
Oikura's assertion was that this should be taken
as some sort of dishonest act happening.

00:21:12.440 --> 00:21:16.310
That someone obtained the math exam questions
from the teachers' office

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:20.190
and discreetly used the contents of the exam
during the study group.

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:25.570
That was why the scores of the students
that joined the study group were all higher.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:26.200
JULY 15 (THU) DAILY DUTIES: KOUMA/MARIZUMI

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:31.660
If there was someone who disgraced
the holy study group, as well as the sacred final exam,

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:33.830
that's something that cannot be forgiven.

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:38.590
Those that did not attend the study group
shouldn't feel that this has nothing to do with you, either.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:42.220
This is an issue involving all of us,
the entirety of class 1-3.

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:44.090
I repeat—

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:52.270
Until we figure out the culprit,
or until the culprit speaks up on his own behalf,

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:56.350
I won't allow anyone out of this classroom.
Prepare yourselves for that.

00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:56.600
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:21:58.020 --> 00:21:59.400
That means, after that,

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:04.030
Oikura-senpai handed over the role
of presiding over the assembly to you?

00:22:04.400 --> 00:22:08.700
The story was that you were the one
presiding over the assembly, correct?

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:11.490
Yeah, that's right.
That's where the presiding member changed.

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:12.080
PRESIDING MEMBER - KOYOMI ARARAGI

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:14.750
Why were you appointed to do so, Araragi-senpai?

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:15.210
CLASS 1-3 SEATING CHART

00:22:15.210 --> 00:22:19.250
You realize that it would be bad for someone
who was part of the study group to preside over this, right?

00:22:19.420 --> 00:22:22.760
That said, you can't say that just anyone
of those that remain can do the job, either.

00:22:23.050 --> 00:22:26.430
After all, at the center of the issue
was the math exam.

00:22:26.720 --> 00:22:29.760
You can't avoid inspecting the exam questions
as a topic for the debate.

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:35.270
That would mean that someone who doesn't
have a high math score can't preside either, right?

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:38.270
Sure, well... I guess that would be so?

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:40.650
But, those who were absent
from the study group;

00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:43.780
those who chose not to go
to the study group in the first place,

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:47.530
their scores were on average 20 points
below those that went, right?

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:50.580
Is there such a person
among those that didn't go,

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:53.330
someone who scored well enough
to match those that did?

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:55.080
Of course there is.

00:22:55.080 --> 00:23:01.290
But, I was the only one that scored better
than every single student that was in the study group.

00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:05.800
That's why I was chosen
to preside over the assembly.

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:06.800
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:08.170
<i>One hundred percent.</i>

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:08.510
KOYOMI ARARAGI

00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:10.850
<i>A score of 100, when the perfect score is 100.</i>

00:23:10.850 --> 00:23:14.680
<i>That was my score in mathematics
on the final exam.</i>

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:18.810
Now, let's have you
move this along quickly, Araragi.

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:23.360
I think it came across already,

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:26.650
but the reason why Class President Oikura
hates me to a psychotic extent

00:23:26.650 --> 00:23:28.700
is because I was good at math.

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:33.080
She had strong conviction that the reason
why nobody called her "Euler" was because of me;

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:38.120
KOYOMI ARARAGI

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:39.290
Then...

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:43.250
To start, everyone that was part of the study group,
please raise your hand.

00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:49.880
As a result, it became clear that there were
19 students that were part of the study group.

00:23:49.880 --> 00:23:50.350
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:56.730
But that means you were able to
narrow it down to 19 suspects.

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:58.480
This gets me excited.

00:23:58.480 --> 00:24:02.560
Well, saying something like that
is imprudent and might need repentance.

00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:06.190
I'll say it right now, Ougi.

00:24:06.610 --> 00:24:09.740
The culprit will not be determined
in this class assembly.

00:24:10.660 --> 00:24:12.780
The situation gets as grim
as it can get,

00:24:12.780 --> 00:24:16.450
and well, everyone gets worn out
and it ends without anyone figuring anything out.

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:17.450
And then...

00:24:18.580 --> 00:24:19.750
Oh, so that's it!

00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:24.630
I figured out how we can escape
from this classroom, Araragi-senpai.

00:24:25.460 --> 00:24:29.510
In other words, by now solving this incident
that remained unsolved two years ago,

00:24:29.510 --> 00:24:32.220
we can get out of here.

00:24:33.510 --> 00:24:34.720
What do you mean by that?

00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:39.060
"Until we figure out the culprit,
I won't allow anyone out of this classroom,"

00:24:39.060 --> 00:24:40.940
is what Oikura-senpai said, right?

00:24:41.230 --> 00:24:44.940
Reversing that, if we can determine
the culprit of that incident,

00:24:44.940 --> 00:24:48.360
we can escape from this room.
That's what this means, right?

00:24:49.940 --> 00:24:54.530
The regrets in the hearts of the students
in class 1-3 back then

00:24:54.530 --> 00:24:57.120
probably materialized in the void
within this school.

00:24:57.660 --> 00:25:00.250
If anything, I guess you can say
this is the ghost of the class assembly.

00:25:00.250 --> 00:25:02.290
The ghost of the class assembly...

00:25:02.290 --> 00:25:08.420
Are you saying I've been trapped by something
as incomprehensible as that? Why me?

00:25:08.420 --> 00:25:09.420
Who knows?

00:25:09.420 --> 00:25:15.120
It could be that you were the one
who took this the most to heart. Perhaps so.

00:25:15.120 --> 00:25:15.850
JULY 15 (THU)

00:25:15.850 --> 00:25:19.250
Because Araragi-senpai,
your life drastically changed on that day.

00:25:20.390 --> 00:25:21.600
Drastically changed...

00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:25.610
Ever since that day,
you've avoided thinking about that incident.

00:25:25.610 --> 00:25:26.820
You've been evading it.

00:25:26.820 --> 00:25:28.980
There hasn't been a day
where you've forgotten about it,

00:25:28.980 --> 00:25:31.190
but there also isn't a day
where you've thought about it.

00:25:31.860 --> 00:25:35.320
But it has finally come -
the day to face your past.

00:25:36.120 --> 00:25:38.370
The time for you to unravel all the mysteries.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:41.540
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:25:41.540 --> 00:25:42.290
KEIRI ASHINE

00:25:42.290 --> 00:25:43.040
MICHISADA IGAMI

00:25:43.040 --> 00:25:43.790
SODACHI OIKURA

00:25:43.790 --> 00:25:44.540
ENJI KIKIGOE

00:25:44.540 --> 00:25:45.290
HOKA KIJIKIRI

00:25:45.290 --> 00:25:46.040
AIZU KUBE

00:25:46.040 --> 00:25:46.790
NAGEKI GEKIZAKA

00:25:46.790 --> 00:25:47.540
SOUSHO KOUDOU

00:25:47.540 --> 00:25:48.290
TSUUMA SHUUI

00:25:48.290 --> 00:25:49.020
JUUDO SHUZAWA

00:25:49.020 --> 00:25:49.780
KOKUSHI SUUCHI

00:25:49.780 --> 00:25:50.540
KIICHIGO DAINO

00:25:50.540 --> 00:25:51.280
CHOUKA NAGAGUTSU

00:25:51.280 --> 00:25:52.050
ROKA HAGA

00:25:52.050 --> 00:25:52.800
SEKIROU HIGUMA

00:25:52.800 --> 00:25:53.550
JOURO HISHIGATA

00:25:53.550 --> 00:25:54.300
SHIJIMA FUDOU

00:25:54.300 --> 00:25:55.050
KABE MADOMURA

00:25:55.050 --> 00:25:55.800
SHOUKEI YOKI

00:25:55.800 --> 00:25:56.800
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:25:57.050 --> 00:25:59.930
After that, what happened to the class assembly?

00:26:00.890 --> 00:26:03.060
When we figured out the names
of the 19 people,

00:26:03.060 --> 00:26:08.980
someone named Arikure complained that
the culprit may not necessarily be one of the 19.

00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:10.440
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:26:10.650 --> 00:26:12.940
So even if they weren't
part of the study group,

00:26:12.940 --> 00:26:15.940
everyone who had a high score
should be added to the suspects list.

00:26:15.940 --> 00:26:16.280
MIAWA MEBE 95
SEIKO HAYAMACHI 92
HITAGI SENJYOGAHARA 98
OKITADA KOUMA 99
KOYOMI ARARAGI 100

00:26:16.280 --> 00:26:20.450
Then, Araragi-senpai, you were tossed
into the suspect list as well?

00:26:20.450 --> 00:26:22.200
I guess that's what happened.

00:26:22.500 --> 00:26:24.080
And, after that?

00:26:24.410 --> 00:26:25.200
After that, Marizumi

00:26:25.200 --> 00:26:26.200
HYOUI MARIZUMI

00:26:26.210 --> 00:26:30.710
objected, saying it was suspect as to whether
such a study group happened to begin with.

00:26:30.960 --> 00:26:33.710
That's rather fundamental, to say...

00:26:33.710 --> 00:26:34.090
STUDY GROUP

00:26:34.090 --> 00:26:37.840
But right afterwards, there was a statement
that the study group was indeed held.

00:26:38.350 --> 00:26:41.220
Sunahama, the one assigned to daily duties
on the day of the math exam, came to school early.

00:26:41.220 --> 00:26:42.220
RUISE SUNAHAMA

00:26:42.220 --> 00:26:45.980
Apparently, she had to clean up after the study group
that left the classroom in a disarray.

00:26:46.230 --> 00:26:47.480
Clean up?

00:26:47.810 --> 00:26:50.520
Like lining the desks back up again,
erasing the chalkboard,

00:26:50.520 --> 00:26:53.230
taking out the trash
from all the snacks, she said.

00:26:53.650 --> 00:26:55.110
Tetsujo, who also came to school early
helped her out, apparently.

00:26:55.110 --> 00:26:56.110
KOMICHI TETSUJO

00:26:57.530 --> 00:26:59.740
What other arguments were made?

00:26:59.740 --> 00:27:00.080
MATH

00:27:00.080 --> 00:27:01.580
Well, if I recall...

00:27:01.580 --> 00:27:02.490
If someone were to secretly pass on
the model answers to the study group...

00:27:02.490 --> 00:27:05.740
FINAL EXAMS

00:27:05.750 --> 00:27:09.250
In reality, if someone were to do that,
someone would be sure to notice, Higuma said.

00:27:09.250 --> 00:27:10.250
SEKIROU HIGUMA

00:27:10.590 --> 00:27:13.510
He said that if something like that happened,
something somewhere would seem a bit forced.

00:27:13.670 --> 00:27:15.750
I see. That is a valid point.

00:27:15.750 --> 00:27:15.970
OIKURA DID NOT ALLOW THAT.

00:27:15.970 --> 00:27:16.630
And then, Oikura...

00:27:16.630 --> 00:27:17.760
SHE WAS PERSISTENT ABOUT CONTINUING THIS
"FIGURING OUT THE CULPRIT" ORDEAL.

00:27:18.010 --> 00:27:22.260
Then, from here, we can verify
the specific contents of the exam questions.

00:27:22.430 --> 00:27:24.140
Seeing how much overlap there is

00:27:24.140 --> 00:27:27.230
between the problems in the study group
and the actual exam questions

00:27:27.230 --> 00:27:30.520
should be determined based on the statements
from every member of the study group.

00:27:30.520 --> 00:27:31.690
AND THEN, WE WILL DETERMINE THE CULPRIT.

00:27:31.690 --> 00:27:33.150
I WON'T ALLOW ANYONE OUT OF THE CLASSROOM.

00:27:33.150 --> 00:27:34.150
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:27:34.150 --> 00:27:40.150
Being in the center of such ugly arguments,
meandering debates, and wasteful exchanges...

00:27:40.150 --> 00:27:45.360
Araragi-senpai, you must have gotten sick
of organisms called human beings.

00:27:47.200 --> 00:27:48.030
That's not it.

00:27:48.320 --> 00:27:48.910
Oh?

00:27:49.240 --> 00:27:54.790
Ougi. What I felt despair about
wasn't the debate, but the outcome.

00:27:54.790 --> 00:27:56.370
THE FEELING THAT WE WERE MAKING THE CORRECT DEBATE
WAS OUT THERE SOMEWHERE.

00:27:56.620 --> 00:27:59.370
Nobody had thought that the outcome
would be like that.

00:27:59.830 --> 00:28:04.130
In pursuit of the just,
we made a definitive mistake.

00:28:04.420 --> 00:28:07.630
And at that moment,
I had lost sight of my own sense of justice.

00:28:08.090 --> 00:28:09.340
The outcome?

00:28:09.340 --> 00:28:12.640
But the outcome was that
you didn't know who the culprit was, right?

00:28:13.300 --> 00:28:17.390
It's true that if the outcome of the debate is such,
you'd surely feel that everything was pointless.

00:28:17.390 --> 00:28:20.650
But it's not enough to feel despair about it, right?

00:28:21.440 --> 00:28:24.730
Yeah. That's right.
We never figured out who the culprit was...

00:28:24.730 --> 00:28:27.400
But it wasn't that
we didn't specify someone as one.

00:28:27.740 --> 00:28:28.530
Huh?

00:28:28.530 --> 00:28:34.080
That's the cause for despair.
The truth that even the unknown can be decided...

00:28:34.240 --> 00:28:36.040
That was why I felt despair.

00:28:36.040 --> 00:28:37.540
I DON'T NEED ANY FRIENDS.

00:28:37.830 --> 00:28:40.540
I see... I see... I see...

00:28:40.830 --> 00:28:42.290
Then, Araragi-senpai.

00:28:42.710 --> 00:28:45.550
I'd like you to tell me what happened after that.

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:48.880
The time to leave school
is coming up soon, isn't it?

00:28:50.430 --> 00:28:55.350
You held a debate for over two hours in a locked room,
and everyone should be at their mental limits.

00:28:55.760 --> 00:29:00.230
And in that critical moment...
What kind of conclusion did you all come up with?

00:29:00.440 --> 00:29:02.810
Where did you guys end up?

00:29:04.690 --> 00:29:08.110
This is staying on my mind.
What happened?

00:29:08.110 --> 00:29:10.400
Even if there are all sorts
of twists and turns,

00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:13.370
somehow overcoming the many obstacles
and the confusion from rubbish,

00:29:13.370 --> 00:29:17.450
if everyone, every single one,
fully becomes happy, I'd like that!

00:29:19.790 --> 00:29:21.960
IT'S TRUE THAT WE WEREN'T ABLE TO BECOME HAPPY—

00:29:22.120 --> 00:29:25.040
IF SO, BACK THEN,
WHAT IN THE WORLD HAD WE BECOME?

00:29:25.630 --> 00:29:28.380
OUGI FORMULA, PART TWO

00:29:28.380 --> 00:29:29.880
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:29:30.220 --> 00:29:34.010
I've had enough. This is too tedious.
Let's just say I did it and end this debate.

00:29:34.010 --> 00:29:38.260
You starting to say stuff like that is out of the question.
Are you covering for someone?

00:29:38.260 --> 00:29:39.810
You must know who the culprit is, then!

00:29:39.810 --> 00:29:41.640
In the first place, is there really a culprit?

00:29:41.640 --> 00:29:44.690
We started talking on the assumption that there is one.
Don't bring that up again.

00:29:44.690 --> 00:29:50.110
No, as a real question, is someone that would steal
exam questions from the teachers' office really among us?

00:29:50.110 --> 00:29:53.860
Before we start talking about ethics,
it's more about whether or not that is physically possible.

00:29:53.860 --> 00:29:55.370
No, I'm talking about whether or not
there's enough guts to do that.

00:29:55.370 --> 00:29:56.280
Are you guys stupid?

00:29:56.280 --> 00:29:59.240
Is there any meaning to having such a debate?
Everyone is just lying.

00:29:59.240 --> 00:30:00.120
I can't bear to listen to this.

00:30:00.120 --> 00:30:02.160
Nowadays, they make exam questions
on computers and stuff, right?

00:30:02.160 --> 00:30:03.580
I'm sorry, can I ask you all to raise your hand
before speaking from hereon?

00:30:03.580 --> 00:30:05.580
you can hack your way in
or something to steal them, can't you?

00:30:05.580 --> 00:30:06.500
You've been watching too many dramas.

00:30:06.500 --> 00:30:11.050
I'll repeat myself, but I think it was Oikura
that was teaching the last problem during the study group.

00:30:11.050 --> 00:30:12.050
Though I can't be sure of it.

00:30:12.050 --> 00:30:14.050
Don't say anything that you can't be sure of.

00:30:14.050 --> 00:30:16.760
Can you hold responsibility
if you ruin someone's life because of it?

00:30:16.760 --> 00:30:18.890
You've always been like that, too.

00:30:19.510 --> 00:30:20.890
Please raise your hand.

00:30:20.890 --> 00:30:22.810
You know, I want to go home already.

00:30:22.810 --> 00:30:25.440
Can you do debates like this
somewhere that I'm not around?

00:30:25.440 --> 00:30:26.690
I won't let you go home.

00:30:26.690 --> 00:30:28.650
If you go home, they might make you
into the culprit, you know?

00:30:28.650 --> 00:30:29.190
That's fine with me.

00:30:29.190 --> 00:30:31.070
I'm sorry, everyone, can you all please calm down.
Let's all regain our cool.

00:30:31.070 --> 00:30:32.690
Why are you acting so tough?

00:30:32.690 --> 00:30:34.280
Like this is something we can stay cool about!

00:30:34.280 --> 00:30:35.240
Please raise your hand to speak—

00:30:35.240 --> 00:30:39.240
In the first place, Araragi got 100%
so this is a test that can be solved, right?

00:30:39.240 --> 00:30:41.750
Why are we talking about cheating or dishonest acts?
It's nonsense.

00:30:41.750 --> 00:30:44.790
You've been quiet all this time,
but what do you think about this, Senjyogahara?

00:30:44.790 --> 00:30:46.000
I'm not quite sure.

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:47.960
Hey guys, I have something I want to say.

00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:49.170
Save it for later!

00:30:49.170 --> 00:30:51.300
Araragi, keep this progressing properly.

00:30:51.300 --> 00:30:53.010
You say that, but...

00:30:53.590 --> 00:30:56.510
In the first place, why did we
hold a study group for just math?

00:30:56.510 --> 00:30:59.640
If there was one for history,
then I would have joined up.

00:30:59.640 --> 00:31:03.600
Of course it's because it looks bad for
the math teacher if her homeroom class

00:31:03.600 --> 00:31:05.440
had a terrible average score for math.

00:31:05.440 --> 00:31:06.770
In other words, it's just for vanity.

00:31:06.770 --> 00:31:09.060
It's what you can call
Miss Class President racking up brownie points.

00:31:09.060 --> 00:31:10.860
That's not the reason at all.

00:31:10.860 --> 00:31:14.530
It is because mathematics
is the most beautiful subject in all academics.

00:31:14.530 --> 00:31:16.400
You're the only one that thinks that.

00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:19.620
What's this about beauty?
So it really is just your convenience after all.

00:31:19.620 --> 00:31:21.740
You can't understand the beauty of mathematics?

00:31:21.740 --> 00:31:22.490
Damn you!

00:31:22.490 --> 00:31:23.660
Please refrain from fighting.

00:31:23.660 --> 00:31:24.290
We're not fighting.
It's because he started saying weird stuff...

00:31:24.290 --> 00:31:25.500
I have an alibi!

00:31:25.500 --> 00:31:26.830
We can't even determine when it was done,
how can you have an alibi?

00:31:26.830 --> 00:31:28.380
Like it was weird for me to be in this high school.

00:31:28.380 --> 00:31:28.500
I have a witness. There is someone
that would guarantee that I'd never do such a thing.

00:31:28.500 --> 00:31:30.250
I didn't go that far!

00:31:31.840 --> 00:31:35.420
We can't keep this going anymore.
This has gotten out of control.

00:31:35.920 --> 00:31:38.890
Give me a break, Oikura. I can't handle this.

00:31:38.890 --> 00:31:41.220
Let's end this before it gets any worse.

00:31:41.220 --> 00:31:43.100
What are you whining about?

00:31:43.100 --> 00:31:46.180
You got a better score than I did,
and you're going to give up?

00:31:46.180 --> 00:31:49.060
Yeah, I'm going to give up. It's impossible.

00:31:49.060 --> 00:31:52.440
Until we figure out the culprit...
I won't allow anyone to go home.

00:31:52.440 --> 00:31:54.730
You can't do such a thing.

00:31:54.730 --> 00:31:57.650
When the chime to leave campus sounds,
we're all going to go home.

00:31:57.650 --> 00:31:59.280
You have a proper understanding of that, right?

00:32:02.660 --> 00:32:06.790
<i>I had forgotten...
just how much Oikura harbored a hatred for me.</i>

00:32:08.750 --> 00:32:10.540
I detest you.

00:32:10.540 --> 00:32:12.630
Stuff like that is where you're terrible at.

00:32:12.630 --> 00:32:14.670
Huh? That's my line!

00:32:16.210 --> 00:32:18.630
Then we shouldn't have
held a study group to begin with!

00:32:18.630 --> 00:32:19.550
Studying is something you—

00:32:19.550 --> 00:32:20.300
Everyone!

00:32:30.230 --> 00:32:33.360
I think we've done
more than enough debating.

00:32:33.940 --> 00:32:36.190
So, I would like to take a vote now.

00:32:36.990 --> 00:32:40.200
Who is the culprit?
We will decide by majority rule.

00:32:40.200 --> 00:32:41.200
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:32:41.450 --> 00:32:44.450
Oh, huh... So that's what you meant.

00:32:44.700 --> 00:32:46.870
That's when the majority
of the class raised their hands,

00:32:46.870 --> 00:32:50.210
and Araragi-senpai, you were
made out to be the culprit, right?

00:32:50.210 --> 00:32:51.210
No.

00:32:51.620 --> 00:32:54.590
The only person that raised their hand
to vote for me was Oikura.

00:32:55.800 --> 00:32:59.420
The majority of the class raised their hands
for attendance number 6...

00:32:59.720 --> 00:33:01.340
when it was time for Sodachi Oikura.

00:33:05.220 --> 00:33:08.270
<i>That look of despair on Oikura's face
I saw back then...</i>

00:33:08.270 --> 00:33:10.140
<i>It's something I can't ever forget.</i>

00:33:10.480 --> 00:33:13.770
<i>And to that despair...
I think I got roped in.</i>

00:33:14.810 --> 00:33:19.740
<i>Ever since, whether it be for class or for exams,
she never once showed up to school.</i>

00:33:19.990 --> 00:33:24.910
<i>Her name apparently is listed
on one of the rosters for third-years...</i>

00:33:25.330 --> 00:33:27.790
<i>But I have no idea which class that is.</i>

00:33:28.500 --> 00:33:34.420
<i>Ever since, the tendency to be absent,
the tendency to ditch school, ramped up.</i>

00:33:35.040 --> 00:33:38.300
<i>To attend the school
that Oikura was not attending</i>

00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:42.220
<i>started to give me a sticky feeling,
similar to that of guilt.</i>

00:33:42.760 --> 00:33:49.140
<i>And ever since then, I - to this day -
have not gotten a perfect score in mathematics.</i>

00:33:50.890 --> 00:33:53.190
Is there a need for you
to shoulder so much, though?

00:33:53.650 --> 00:33:59.360
In the first place, it was said that Oikura-senpai
was the front-runner of all suspects.

00:33:59.360 --> 00:34:02.400
That class assembly wasn't something
someone suggested to her.

00:34:02.400 --> 00:34:04.320
It was something she planned on her own.

00:34:05.070 --> 00:34:07.530
If Oikura really was the culprit,

00:34:07.530 --> 00:34:09.740
there wouldn't have been a need
to create such an assembly.

00:34:10.120 --> 00:34:14.580
Just picking up on that one fact,
I can declare that Oikura wasn't the culprit.

00:34:15.750 --> 00:34:18.880
I see... Declare, huh...

00:34:19.920 --> 00:34:23.880
In any case, seeing truth be fabricated
right in front of your eyes...

00:34:23.880 --> 00:34:29.310
Witnessing a stupid conclusion being drawn,
I couldn't contain myself anymore.

00:34:29.720 --> 00:34:31.350
Something in me broke.

00:34:32.100 --> 00:34:35.060
The moment when over half the class -
most of the students -

00:34:35.060 --> 00:34:37.230
raised their hands simultaneously,

00:34:37.230 --> 00:34:39.770
with no prior concerting or conference,
not even making eye contact.

00:34:39.770 --> 00:34:42.110
The moment when truth had been decided...

00:34:42.110 --> 00:34:44.400
The moment when justice had been settled...

00:34:44.950 --> 00:34:49.990
I'd never seen a scary moment like that.
I lost sight at that moment.

00:34:50.540 --> 00:34:54.160
No... I didn't lose sight. I lost it.

00:34:54.830 --> 00:34:58.340
Until that moment,
I had believed in something like righteousness.

00:34:58.670 --> 00:35:04.630
That there were things that were "right" in the world,
and it was about whether or not you could do it. But...

00:35:04.630 --> 00:35:06.010
EVEN IF MISTAKEN, EVEN IF CRUEL, EVEN IF STUPID

00:35:06.010 --> 00:35:07.430
IF MANY PEOPLE ACKNOWLEDGE IT,

00:35:07.430 --> 00:35:08.640
I FOUND OUT THAT IT CAN BECOME THE RIGHT THING.

00:35:08.890 --> 00:35:12.770
I found out that righteousness
was able to be infinitely mass-produced.

00:35:13.350 --> 00:35:16.900
I found out that righteousness
was established by the number of people.

00:35:17.230 --> 00:35:20.020
I found out that maneuvering for a majority
was everything.

00:35:20.520 --> 00:35:23.780
That is why I chose solitude over establishment.

00:35:24.740 --> 00:35:28.280
I don't need friends, because if I make friends,
my strength as a human decreases.

00:35:29.950 --> 00:35:33.540
In order to protect my own righteousness,
that was the only thing I could do.

00:35:34.750 --> 00:35:38.540
This ended up being a long story,
but that is the story of Koyomi Araragi.

00:35:39.330 --> 00:35:41.460
Thank you for listening, Ougi.

00:35:41.460 --> 00:35:44.460
Oh, I guess it really is just like what you said.

00:35:44.460 --> 00:35:48.800
Once I told the story, it really was nothing much,
and it made me feel at east.

00:35:49.140 --> 00:35:50.430
I'm troubled.

00:35:51.760 --> 00:35:56.060
I'm troubled if you feel at ease already,
Araragi-senpai.

00:36:00.980 --> 00:36:04.440
Oikura-senpai wasn't the culprit,
and the story ends?

00:36:04.440 --> 00:36:08.110
That means we can't
leave this classroom after all.

00:36:08.320 --> 00:36:09.780
Have you forgotten?

00:36:09.780 --> 00:36:14.330
In order to leave this classroom,
we need to identify who the culprit is.

00:36:14.490 --> 00:36:16.790
The culprit that could not be identified on that day...

00:36:16.790 --> 00:36:18.330
Not by majority rule....

00:36:19.670 --> 00:36:21.960
We need to determine it ourselves.

00:36:23.710 --> 00:36:27.380
The grudge Oikura had that day
created this classroom, perhaps?

00:36:27.380 --> 00:36:31.720
If so, there is some inevitability
in how I became trapped in here like this.

00:36:31.720 --> 00:36:32.390
OIKURA PERHAPS

00:36:32.390 --> 00:36:33.260
STILL HASN'T FORGIVEN ME?

00:36:33.260 --> 00:36:34.100
JUST LIKE THAT DAY

00:36:34.100 --> 00:36:34.720
DOES SHE STILL HATE ME?

00:36:35.020 --> 00:36:39.350
Well, I think Oikura-senpai
has forgotten about you already, maybe?

00:36:39.350 --> 00:36:41.100
Things usually end up like that,
surprisingly enough.

00:36:41.900 --> 00:36:44.110
Then, what in the world is this classroom—

00:36:44.480 --> 00:36:46.320
Didn't I tell you?

00:36:46.320 --> 00:36:50.820
This was a classroom that your heart created,
Araragi-senpai. That's what I think.

00:36:50.820 --> 00:36:55.370
That's what I'm going to define this as...
a classroom that the heart - a sense of regret - created.

00:36:56.080 --> 00:36:59.120
If, on that day, you were able to pin down
who the culprit was,

00:36:59.120 --> 00:37:01.750
Sodachi Oikura would not have been ruined.

00:37:01.750 --> 00:37:03.880
And you wouldn't have lost your righteousness.

00:37:04.710 --> 00:37:07.380
The classroom was built
on such regrets you have.

00:37:08.130 --> 00:37:11.890
You have always pursued after the righteousness
you had lost that day.

00:37:12.550 --> 00:37:17.020
In order to regain the lost righteousness,
you created this classroom.

00:37:18.020 --> 00:37:19.020
I did?

00:37:19.520 --> 00:37:23.610
<i>Is that possible?
Can I create a classroom like this...</i>

00:37:23.770 --> 00:37:27.030
<i>But, each apparition has a reason befitting it.</i>

00:37:27.030 --> 00:37:32.030
<i>If that's the case, for "me",
this is enough reasoning for this case.</i>

00:37:33.320 --> 00:37:36.580
I guess we have to do
the class assembly over again.

00:37:36.580 --> 00:37:39.830
This time for sure, we need to find the culprit,
no, the true culprit...

00:37:39.830 --> 00:37:42.790
Oh no, we already know
who the true culprit is, right?

00:37:43.960 --> 00:37:48.170
I mean, Araragi-senpai,
you should actually know who it is, too...

00:37:48.420 --> 00:37:52.430
Who was supposed to be denounced
at that class assembly?

00:37:52.430 --> 00:37:56.300
Something like that was obvious
after hearing your story, Araragi-senpai.

00:37:56.760 --> 00:38:02.060
Araragi-senpai, your feeling of "I feel so guilty"
towards Oikura-senpai is needlessly strong

00:38:02.060 --> 00:38:05.690
because subconsciously
you know who the culprit is.

00:38:05.690 --> 00:38:09.070
Otherwise, you'd never tell the story
in the way that you did.

00:38:09.070 --> 00:38:10.690
The way that I did?

00:38:12.700 --> 00:38:15.320
<i>What in the world is this girl talking about?</i>

00:38:15.320 --> 00:38:17.370
<i>What does she actually know?</i>

00:38:18.450 --> 00:38:20.450
I don't know anything.

00:38:20.450 --> 00:38:24.830
You're the one that knows.
Araragi-senpai.... Koyomi Araragi.

00:38:25.170 --> 00:38:26.080
I...

00:38:27.250 --> 00:38:30.380
The great detective gathers everyone
and says, "Well..."

00:38:30.380 --> 00:38:33.720
Since there is no great detective here,
I'll say it in his place.

00:38:33.840 --> 00:38:34.470
Well...

00:38:34.880 --> 00:38:40.720
Burned by her own karma and falling to ruin,
the dull-witted silly fool Sodachi Oikura.

00:38:41.060 --> 00:38:45.230
In order to mourn for her, we shall solemnly go through
with "figuring out the culprit" that she wished for.

00:38:45.940 --> 00:38:47.400
Whoops, this isn't good.

00:38:47.400 --> 00:38:50.230
If this is a "figuring out the culprit",
this is the one thing that must be said.

00:38:50.900 --> 00:38:55.740
Whether it's getting rid of apparitions or solving mysteries,
proper etiquette is important.

00:38:55.990 --> 00:38:58.370
I challenge all you readers.

00:38:58.990 --> 00:39:00.490
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:39:01.160 --> 00:39:03.250
The culprit is Komichi Tetsujo.

00:39:05.080 --> 00:39:06.330
Shall I continue?

00:39:06.880 --> 00:39:07.830
Yeah.

00:39:08.880 --> 00:39:11.000
Why did you think Tetsujo was suspicious?

00:39:11.710 --> 00:39:15.720
Right when you entered the classroom,
I commented on how all the seats were filled.

00:39:15.720 --> 00:39:20.680
You said that if we were to be precise,
Oikura-senpai's seat was empty.

00:39:20.680 --> 00:39:22.390
That's how you replied.

00:39:22.390 --> 00:39:24.600
But, don't you find this strange?

00:39:24.600 --> 00:39:26.770
Araragi-senpai, your seat has to be empty as well.

00:39:27.310 --> 00:39:29.400
Was someone sitting there?

00:39:30.110 --> 00:39:32.650
For instance, the homeroom teacher?

00:39:33.280 --> 00:39:34.320
SO, ARARAGI-SENPAI, IT WASN'T THAT
YOU WEREN'T PERMITTED TO SIT DOWN BY OIKURA-SENPAI,

00:39:34.320 --> 00:39:35.280
BUT PERHAPS YOU WEREN'T ABLE
TO SIT DOWN IN THE FIRST PLACE.

00:39:35.570 --> 00:39:39.370
But, that said, that doesn't automatically mean
that Tetsujo is the culprit.

00:39:39.370 --> 00:39:43.160
When the meeting became very complicated,
someone had mentioned

00:39:43.160 --> 00:39:45.790
that the homeroom teacher for class 1-3
was a math teacher.

00:39:46.160 --> 00:39:49.250
That position is not merely someone
who knows about the problems beforehand.

00:39:49.250 --> 00:39:51.040
She is the one that creates the problems.

00:39:51.290 --> 00:39:55.760
If so, she can just create exam problems
based on what the study group had covered.

00:39:57.010 --> 00:39:59.260
Sunahama-senpai,
who had the daily duties the next day,

00:39:59.260 --> 00:40:03.770
had whined about having to clean up
after the study group early in the morning.

00:40:03.770 --> 00:40:07.140
And that Komichi Tetsujo
had helped her out with it.

00:40:07.350 --> 00:40:09.310
What kind of cleanup work was it?

00:40:09.650 --> 00:40:13.230
Hey, hey, Araragi-senpai,
what kind of cleanup work was it?

00:40:14.110 --> 00:40:16.780
Throwing away snack bags, realigning desks...

00:40:16.780 --> 00:40:17.950
The one that's not those!

00:40:20.570 --> 00:40:22.910
And erasing the chalkboards and stuff, right?

00:40:23.660 --> 00:40:26.910
<i>Of course, they must have been writing and erasing,
and writing and erasing.</i>

00:40:26.910 --> 00:40:29.670
<i>So not everything could be deciphered.</i>

00:40:30.540 --> 00:40:33.750
But I guess you can read through
at least a part of it, huh.

00:40:33.750 --> 00:40:34.420
Yes.

00:40:34.420 --> 00:40:34.670
(WED)

00:40:34.670 --> 00:40:36.170
And if Komichi Tetsujo
is the homeroom teacher,

00:40:36.170 --> 00:40:37.340
(THU)

00:40:37.340 --> 00:40:37.920
she can create exam problems that go along
with what the study group had studied.

00:40:37.920 --> 00:40:41.550
DETAILS:
1. LOCATION - CLASS 1-3 CLASSROOM
2. DATE - JULY 7 (WED) 15:00~18:00
3. SUBJECT - MATH III,C
PLEASE CONTACT OIKURA FOR DETAILS ON HOW TO JOIN.

00:40:41.890 --> 00:40:44.140
Of course, it's the actual day of the test,

00:40:44.140 --> 00:40:48.020
so even if she were able to correct the exam problems,
she probably only got a part of the exam fixed.

00:40:51.520 --> 00:40:54.070
What else... I guess the motive?

00:40:54.070 --> 00:40:57.360
The motivation behind committing the crime.
The reason why she did such a thing.

00:40:58.030 --> 00:41:00.700
Ougi, you even know that as well?

00:41:02.200 --> 00:41:06.120
If the culprit was a student,
this would be a crime that makes absolutely no sense.

00:41:06.330 --> 00:41:08.250
If the overall scores
of the entire class went up,

00:41:08.250 --> 00:41:11.750
that means that, relatively speaking,
the deviation value for each person will go down.

00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:17.380
However, with the entire class getting better scores,
there is someone whose assessment becomes better.

00:41:18.880 --> 00:41:21.550
That is the math teacher.

00:41:21.550 --> 00:41:25.260
She'll be assessed as having high skills
in instruction and guidance.

00:41:26.890 --> 00:41:29.310
Is there anything else, Araragi-senpai?

00:41:30.640 --> 00:41:31.520
There isn't.

00:41:32.060 --> 00:41:35.520
I see. Then, we should probably be on our way.

00:41:38.320 --> 00:41:40.530
You can leave now, Araragi-senpai.

00:41:40.860 --> 00:41:41.910
Yeah...

00:41:46.200 --> 00:41:47.740
What do you mean, I can leave now?

00:41:47.740 --> 00:41:48.450
Huh?

00:41:48.450 --> 00:41:51.670
Well, I thought that was
a weird way to say it, so...

00:41:51.670 --> 00:41:52.670
What did you mean?

00:41:52.870 --> 00:41:55.250
Oh, you didn't know?

00:41:55.250 --> 00:42:00.800
Vampires often are unable to enter buildings or rooms
unless the person inside authorizes them to.

00:42:01.010 --> 00:42:04.180
Ah... Though I've never
had an experience like that.

00:42:04.430 --> 00:42:07.350
Well, well... Ms. Shinobu is a special one,

00:42:07.350 --> 00:42:10.930
and we had the pattern not where we couldn't go in,
but one where we couldn't leave.

00:42:10.930 --> 00:42:13.230
That's why I phrased it as
"you can leave now."

00:42:13.230 --> 00:42:15.690
It was something like a magic spell
to ease one's mind.

00:42:16.150 --> 00:42:20.690
That's as if you were the one
that trapped me in here, Ougi.

00:42:20.940 --> 00:42:25.450
That's a misunderstanding.
I would never trap you in, Araragi-senpai.

00:42:25.450 --> 00:42:28.330
There's no way I would do such a thing.

00:42:28.580 --> 00:42:32.370
Araragi-senpai, you were
trapped in your own past.

00:42:32.370 --> 00:42:35.460
All this time, for two years.
Isn't that right?

00:42:37.130 --> 00:42:39.050
I do sympathize, though.

00:42:39.050 --> 00:42:42.300
A teacher, who is the symbol
of righteousness to a student,

00:42:42.300 --> 00:42:44.630
was the one behaving dishonestly...

00:42:44.630 --> 00:42:46.390
That feels like betrayal,

00:42:46.390 --> 00:42:49.970
and you can't help it if you, Araragi-senpai,
decided to put a lid on your heart.

00:42:50.350 --> 00:42:54.640
Is the fact that Oikura, despite not having attended
enough days, keeps moving up to the next class...

00:42:54.640 --> 00:42:57.980
Is that something along the lines
of atonement from Mrs. Tetsujo?

00:42:58.480 --> 00:43:04.990
Atonement? That's not it. It's an excuse.
She just wants to believe that she's a decent human.

00:43:23.260 --> 00:43:24.880
Why I felt despair...

00:43:25.220 --> 00:43:28.050
Now, next. Attendance number 6.

00:43:28.050 --> 00:43:32.140
If you think I, Sodachi Oikura, am the culprit,
please raise your hand.

00:43:32.930 --> 00:43:35.310
<i>Why I felt despair against righteousness,</i>

00:43:35.310 --> 00:43:39.150
<i>was that back then, blending into the classmates
that designated Oikura as the culprit,</i>

00:43:39.610 --> 00:43:44.610
<i>Tetsujo, a teacher, had been
holding up her hand straight up as well.</i>

00:44:01.590 --> 00:44:03.090
OWARIMONOGATARI
OUGI FORMULA

00:44:05.840 --> 00:44:12.600
<i>The next day, on a whim, I decided to stop by
the audiovisual room on my way to my classroom.</i>

00:44:12.930 --> 00:44:16.100
<i>To be precise, to the spot
next to the audiovisual room.</i>

00:44:17.600 --> 00:44:21.360
<i>As expected, there was no such thing there
as an empty classroom.</i>

00:44:21.520 --> 00:44:26.360
<i>Moreover, there was no dead space whatsoever
along the lines of what Ougi had drawn in her notebook.</i>

00:44:28.030 --> 00:44:29.860
<i>There was nothing here.</i>

00:44:30.870 --> 00:44:32.740
<i>Nothing had happened here.</i>

00:44:33.490 --> 00:44:38.250
<i>The secret room, the locked room,
the figuring out the culprit, the unexpected truth...</i>

00:44:38.250 --> 00:44:40.630
<i>The class assembly, and the majority rule.</i>

00:44:41.040 --> 00:44:44.630
<i>Everything was in the past,
and everything was already done and over.</i>

00:44:47.880 --> 00:44:51.390
<i>Within this teachers' office,
Komichi Tetsujo does not exist.</i>

00:44:51.680 --> 00:44:55.640
<i>That said, it's not that she quit being a teacher
because she suffered from a guilty conscience,</i>

00:44:55.640 --> 00:44:58.180
<i>nor that she was fired
after her dishonest act was found out.</i>

00:44:58.180 --> 00:44:58.890
<i>It's nothing like that.</i>

00:44:58.890 --> 00:45:00.150
KOMICHI TETSUJO - MATERNITY LEAVE

00:45:00.150 --> 00:45:04.570
<i>The occasion was that she got pregnant,
and was on maternity leave. What a joyous occasion.</i>

00:45:04.980 --> 00:45:08.990
<i>She probably won't be
back at school before I graduate,</i>

00:45:08.990 --> 00:45:12.490
<i>so I'll probably never
see Tetsujo again in my life.</i>

00:45:12.950 --> 00:45:14.950
<i>And about that, I feel nothing.</i>

00:45:15.120 --> 00:45:20.620
<i>In the first place, for me, after seeing her from behind,
raising her hand on that day two years ago...</i>

00:45:20.620 --> 00:45:23.880
<i>she was no longer a teacher,
or an adult.</i>

00:45:28.010 --> 00:45:30.010
Oh, morning, Araragi.

00:45:30.010 --> 00:45:32.090
Oh, morning, Hanekawa.

00:45:32.260 --> 00:45:33.600
Bad timing.

00:45:33.800 --> 00:45:34.350
What?

00:45:34.600 --> 00:45:37.600
Araragi, I don't think you should
enter the classroom right now.

00:45:38.480 --> 00:45:39.350
Heave-ho!

00:45:42.350 --> 00:45:43.520
Araragi.

00:45:43.730 --> 00:45:47.280
Had you noticed that there was
an empty seat in our class?

00:45:48.070 --> 00:45:53.660
Yeah, I noticed it, or rather,
I had thought that it was a spare seat. What of it?

00:45:55.240 --> 00:45:59.250
What, are you trying to tell me
that a ghost was sitting there today when you arrived?

00:45:59.250 --> 00:46:00.540
Is that what this is about?

00:46:00.540 --> 00:46:03.920
I'll tell you something.
Something like a mere ghost won't scare me one bit.

00:46:04.130 --> 00:46:07.420
The one sitting there wasn't a ghost.
It was a human.

00:46:08.460 --> 00:46:13.430
A classmate who had not come to school
for the longest time suddenly came to school today.

00:46:13.890 --> 00:46:15.430
Oh, I see.

00:46:15.930 --> 00:46:19.810
Then, that seat was...
that person's seat, huh?

00:46:19.810 --> 00:46:22.890
That's surprising that there was
one more classmate in my class.

00:46:24.690 --> 00:46:28.400
But, why does that make it
so I shouldn't enter the classroom?

00:46:29.190 --> 00:46:31.400
Because it's Ms. Oikura.

00:46:34.030 --> 00:46:35.870
Sodachi Oikura...

00:46:35.870 --> 00:46:39.490
She's apparently been home-schooling
for about two years now.

00:46:39.490 --> 00:46:42.830
She came to school
as if she was switching places with Mrs. Tetsujo.

00:46:43.420 --> 00:48:26.351
Araragi, you didn't get along with her, if I recall?
